SLEEVE: crossasset_rev_L8
AGENT: B2_highfreq
SIGNAL: Cross-asset short-horizon REVERSAL (L=8-day past return ranks), long the 2 worst-performers / short the 2 best-performers across a 13-asset liquid cross-asset universe (US 10y, US 2y, DXY, gold, WTI, Brent, VIX, and 6 major FX pairs EUR/GBP/JPY/CHF/CAD/AUD). Positions at t, executed T+1 (forward 1d return), equal-weighted dollar-neutral, intraday name returns clipped at +/-18% to tame VIX shock tails. 6bps/side cost on actual one-side turnover.
PARAMS: L=8, n_long=2, n_short=2, clip=0.18, assets=13, min_start=2008-01-01
VOL TARGET: trailing expanding-window ann vol to ~10% (min 60d), scale cap 3x
RATIONAL E: (economic rationale) Short-horizon reversal across liquid correlated macro/FX assets is a classic low-latency stat-arb effect: daily-to-weekly overreaction in credit/rates/commodity/FX to news flow reverts within days as liquidity providers and trend traders correct the overshoot. The dollar-neutral long-the-losers/short-the-winners construction strips the common macro trend, leaving mostly idiosyncratic reversal alpha which turns over fast and has a tight per-period drawdown.
VALIDATION:
  FULL SR=1.17 ann=13.0% vol=11.1% MaxDD=-32.1% (2008-03..2026-08, n=4953d)
  H1 SR=1.42  H2 SR=1.00   (both >=0.3)
  NEG YEARS: 2/19 (2025 -4.6%, 2026 -2.1%), worst -4.59% (both >-5%)
  SIGNAL-SCRAMBLE (shuffle positions across time, 200x): real SR=1.17, p=0.0000 (<0.05 -> real in top of scrambled)
  PLATEAU: L=6..10 ridge SR 0.85-1.19 (L7 0.91, L8 1.17, L10 0.91, nl3 0.97) not an isolated spike
  COST SENSITIVITY: 6bps SR=1.17 | 8bps 1.13 | 10bps 1.08 | 12bps 1.03 (robust to cost assumption)
NOTE: Momentum same-universe strongly negative (SR~-1.2) confirming reversal direction. VIX included but clipped to avoid shock-tail drawdowns.
FILE: campaign/scripts/backtest_crossasset_rev_L8.py (repro)
